<newsitem itemid="47709" id="root" date="1996-09-11" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Christies H1 pretax profit leaps 57 pct.</title>
<headline>Christies H1 pretax profit leaps 57 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		5.94		   vs 3.63</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.2		    vs 0.65</p>
<p> Pretax		     15.89		  vs 10.12</p>
<p> Turnover		   105.59		 vs 91.36</p>
<p>NOTE - UK auction house Christie's International Plc said demand for good quality items remained strong and &quot;important consignments&quot; for the autumn season had been received or were expected for all major auction centres.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	 13.91		  vs 8.37</p>
<p> Interest income	  1.98		   vs 1.75</p>
<p> Tax charge		 5.12		   vs 3.40</p>
<p> Net taxed		  10.77		  vs 6.72</p>
<p> Retained profit	  8.38		   vs 5.24</p>
<p> Pay date		   Oct 25</p>
<p>Div registration date  Oct 1  </p>
<p> Ex-div date		Sept 23</p>
<p>NOTE - Christies said it was confident about the long term future of the art market and in its ability to trade profitably in that market. It noted that dividends were boosted to reduce the disparity between the half year and final payouts &quot;and should not be interpreted as an indication of the likely level of the final dividend&quot;.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
